Subject: [PATCH 0011/0012] let libwayland own the descriptors the stream window sends


The stream window kept every frame descriptor in a list and closed the list
after a flush reported success, because libwayland only copies a descriptor
into the socket when the request that carries it is written. But libwayland
closes each descriptor itself as soon as the request goes out, so that close
was a second close of a number that had been free for a moment already. The
decoder opens a fresh dma-buf descriptor for every frame it exports and this
board's capture pool churns through them at frame rate, so it regularly took
the number back between the two closes: the export then failed with EBADF and
a number the decoder had reused for something else was handed to the
compositor, which refused the import ("Failed to import plane 0 as R8") and
closed the stream window with a protocol error.

The list now only tracks what is still queued; a successful flush forgets the
entries, and a descriptor that never went into a request (a cached wl_buffer,
a frame dropped before the surface) is closed by present() itself.
---
 .../rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp         | 63 ++++++++++++++-----
 .../streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.h | 17 ++---
 2 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp
index f13c5353..8432cd9b 100644
